There's a proposal https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/83998 that says to add the following prologue to cpps/hpps.  Can you add this to all of your new files?

// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright OpenBMC Authors

I'm guessing you have the JSON written a certain way because it matches the docs or makes the most sense that way.

However, just as an FYI, the JSON can contain a simple bool/string/int, an array, or an object.

So you could just have the array without the enclosing object:
```
    const auto sensorConfig = R"(
        [
            {
                "path_suffix": "_0",
                "threshold": 30,
                "has_target": true
            },
            {
                "path_suffix": "_1",
                "threshold": 30,
                "has_target": false,
                "factor": 0.625,
                "offset": 1100
            }
        ]
      )"_json;
```

And then pass that element directly to getSensorDefs().
